# shadcn/ui Component Library - STRICT RULES

**CRITICAL**: This project uses **ONLY** shadcn/ui components for all UI elements. **ABSOLUTELY NO CUSTOM UI COMPONENTS** are allowed in this project.

## 🚫 STRICT PROHIBITIONS

### ❌ NEVER CREATE CUSTOM UI COMPONENTS
- **NO** custom buttons, cards, inputs, or any UI elements
- **NO** custom styling beyond shadcn/ui components
- **NO** custom CSS classes for UI elements
- **NO** custom form components
- **NO** custom modal implementations
- **NO** custom navigation components
- **NO** custom layout components

### ❌ NEVER USE ALTERNATIVE UI LIBRARIES
- **NO** Material-UI, Ant Design, Chakra UI, or other component libraries
- **NO** custom Tailwind component implementations
- **NO** custom styled components

## ✅ MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS

### 1. ONLY Use shadcn/ui Components
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Always use shadcn components
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card";
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input";

// ❌ WRONG - Never create custom components
function CustomButton() { return <button>...</button>; }
```

### 2. Install Missing Components First
Before implementing any UI element, check if a shadcn component exists:
```bash
# Install required components
npx shadcn@latest add button
npx shadcn@latest add card
npx shadcn@latest add input
npx shadcn@latest add dialog
npx shadcn@latest add form
```

### 3. Clerk Authentication Integration
**ALL Clerk authentication must use shadcn/ui components:**

#### Sign In/Sign Up Buttons
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use shadcn Button with Clerk
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

export function AuthButtons() {
  return (
    <div className="flex gap-2">
      <SignInButton mode="modal">
        <Button variant="outline">Sign In</Button>
      </SignInButton>
      <SignUpButton mode="modal">
        <Button>Sign Up</Button>
      </SignUpButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### User Profile Components
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use shadcn components for user profile
import { UserButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Avatar, AvatarFallback, AvatarImage } from "@/components/ui/avatar";

export function UserProfile() {
  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
      <UserButton 
        appearance={{
          elements: {
            avatarBox: "w-8 h-8"
          }
        }}
      />
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### Modal Authentication
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use shadcn Dialog for authentication modals
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Dialog, DialogContent, DialogHeader, DialogTitle, DialogTrigger } from "@/components/ui/dialog";

export function AuthModal() {
  return (
    <Dialog>
      <DialogTrigger asChild>
        <Button variant="outline">Sign In</Button>
      </DialogTrigger>
      <DialogContent>
        <DialogHeader>
          <DialogTitle>Authentication</DialogTitle>
        </DialogHeader>
        <div className="space-y-4">
          <SignInButton mode="modal">
            <Button className="w-full">Sign In</Button>
          </SignInButton>
          <SignUpButton mode="modal">
            <Button variant="outline" className="w-full">Sign Up</Button>
          </SignUpButton>
        </div>
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  );
}
```

## Project Configuration

- **Components Directory**: `@/components` (aliased in [components.json](mdc:components.json))
- **Utils Directory**: `@/lib/utils` (aliased in [components.json](mdc:components.json))
- **Style**: Default shadcn style
- **CSS Variables**: Enabled
- **Base Color**: Slate
- **Tailwind Config**: [tailwind.config.ts](mdc:tailwind.config.ts)
- **Global CSS**: [app/globals.css](mdc:app/globals.css)

## Setup Commands

### Initial Setup (if not already done)
If shadcn is not initialized, use:
```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

### Adding Components
To add a specific component (e.g., button, card, input), use:
```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
npx shadcn@latest add card
npx shadcn@latest add input
npx shadcn@latest add dialog
npx shadcn@latest add form
npx shadcn@latest add avatar
```

## Usage Guidelines

1. **ONLY use shadcn components** - NO exceptions
2. **Check if component exists** before implementing any UI element
3. **Install missing components** using `npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>`
4. **Import components** from `@/components/ui/` directory
5. **Use the utility function** from `@/lib/utils` for className merging (cn function)
6. **Clerk authentication must use shadcn buttons and dialogs**

## Required Components for This Project

### Essential Components
- `button` - For ALL button interactions (including Clerk auth)
- `card` - For content containers
- `input` - For form inputs
- `label` - For form labels
- `textarea` - For multi-line text input
- `select` - For dropdown selections
- `dialog` - For modals and popups (including Clerk auth)
- `form` - For form handling
- `avatar` - For user profile images

### Additional Components
- `toast` - For notifications
- `badge` - For status indicators
- `separator` - For visual dividers
- `skeleton` - For loading states
- `sheet` - For side panels
- `dropdown-menu` - For dropdown menus
- `tabs` - For tabbed interfaces
- `accordion` - For collapsible content

## Enforcement Rules

### Code Review Checklist
Before any commit, verify:
- [ ] No custom UI components created
- [ ] All UI elements use shadcn components
- [ ] Clerk authentication uses shadcn buttons/dialogs
- [ ] No custom CSS classes for UI elements
- [ ] All imports are from `@/components/ui/`

### Violation Consequences
Any custom UI components will be **immediately rejected** and must be replaced with shadcn components.

## Examples of What NOT to Do

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Custom button component
function CustomButton({ children, onClick }) {
  return (
    <button 
      className="bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded"
      onClick={onClick}
    >
      {children}
    </button>
  );
}

// ❌ WRONG - Custom card component
function CustomCard({ children }) {
  return (
    <div className="bg-white shadow-lg rounded-lg p-6">
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}

// ❌ WRONG - Custom form input
function CustomInput({ placeholder }) {
  return (
    <input 
      className="border border-gray-300 rounded px-3 py-2"
      placeholder={placeholder}
    />
  );
}
```

## Examples of What TO Do

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use shadcn components
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card";
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input";

function MyComponent() {
